utations prefer dashboard cron routes. Explicit default-profile queries avoid the dashboard's all-profile list default. Only unsupported routes or an unconfigured keyless token transport permit a legacy fetch."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/dashboard-api-url.ts#dashboardApiUrl]] is the shared, runtime-independent URL builder. Schedule adapters use it without initializing session storage or locale configuration; the session bridge keeps its existing export for callers.","startLine":13,"endLine":13,"text":"src/main/dashboard-api-url.ts#dashboardApiUrl is the shared, runtime-independent URL builder. Schedule adapters use it without initializing session storage or locale configuration; the session bridge keeps its existing export for callers."},{"markdown":"Token dashboard connection tests use public status only for discovery, then verify a protected session-list route with the candidate session-token header. Raw gateway health is public too, so gateway tests verify protected model access with the candidate Bearer token. Existing OAuth discovery remains separate from native sign-in.","startLine":15,"endLine":15,"text":"Token dashboard connection tests use public status only for discovery, then verify a protected session-list route with the candidate session-token header. Raw gateway health is public too, so gateway tests verify protected model access with the candidate Bearer token. Existing OAuth discovery remains separate from native sign-in."},{"markdown":"A fresh Agent 0.23.1 can return a non-HTML session-list 503 before its first session initializes the database. Only that response permits a read-only protected profiles probe with the same candidate headers. Profiles must succeed; authentication denials, other statuses, HTML and network failures never trigger this fallback.","startLine":17,"endLine":17,"text":"A fresh Agent 0.23.1 can return a non-HTML session-list 503 before its first session initializes the database. Only that response permits a read-only protected profiles probe with the same candidate headers. Profiles must succeed; authentication denials, other statuses, HTML and network failures never trigger this fallback."},{"markdown":"Remote token, OAuth and SSH chat readiness verifies protected access before probing the chat WebSocket, including when a fresh Agent has not created its session database.","startLine":21,"endLine":21,"text":"Remote token, OAuth and SSH chat readiness verifies protected access before probing the chat WebSocket, including when a fresh Agent has not created its session database."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/dashboard.ts#verifyDashboardProtectedAccess]] retries only a typed, non-HTML session-list 503 against `/api/profiles` on the identical authenticated transport. Token and SSH retain their session headers; OAuth retains the main-process cookie partition and login-required errors. The fallback never switches credentials, creates a session or uses anonymous HTTP.","startLine":23,"endLine":23,"text":"src/main/dashboard.ts#verifyDashboardProtectedAccess retries only a typed, non-HTML session-list 503 against /api/profiles on the identical authenticated transport. Token and SSH retain their session headers; OAuth retains the main-process cookie partition and login-required errors. The fallback never switches credentials, creates a session or uses anonymous HTTP."},{"markdown":"HTTP errors carry structured status and HTML classification; response text cannot authorize a fallback. A successful profiles probe still requires [[src/main/dashboard.ts#probeDashboardWebSocket]], with a freshly minted ticket for OAuth. HTML, interrupted responses and authentication failures remain errors.","startLine":25,"endLine":25,"text":"HTTP errors carry structured status and HTML classification; response text cannot authorize a fallback. A successful profiles probe still requires src/main/dashboard.ts#probeDashboardWebSocket, with a freshly minted ticket for OAuth. HTML, interrupted responses and authentication failures