 proxies, and never fall back from OAuth failure to bare fetch."},{"markdown":"Remote output requires membership in the job's newest 100-run window before reading session messages. A 500-message page is marked partial; hidden display messages are omitted. The current Agent exposes cron sessions, not script-file output. Servers returning script-preview rows expose only a preview, always marked partial. Local history reads newest regular files without following file symlinks, with bounded previews and a 200,000-character output cap. SSH history is explicitly unsupported.","startLine":35,"endLine":35,"text":"Remote output requires membership in the job's newest 100-run window before reading session messages. A 500-message page is marked partial; hidden display messages are omitted. The current Agent exposes cron sessions, not script-file output. Servers returning script-preview rows expose only a preview, always marked partial. Local history reads newest regular files without following file symlinks, with bounded previews and a 200,000-character output cap. SSH history is explicitly unsupported."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Schedules/CronRunHistory.tsx#CronRunHistory]] cancels obsolete reads on configuration, profile, connection and open-run changes. Refresh reloads both the expanded list and open output. The Layout Schedules key follows connection, profile and semantic settings identity; display-label notifications preserve its pane.","startLine":37,"endLine":37,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Schedules/CronRunHistory.tsx#CronRunHistory cancels obsolete reads on configuration, profile, connection and open-run changes. Refresh reloads both the expanded list and open output. The Layout Schedules key follows connection, profile and semantic settings identity; display-label notifications preserve its pane."},{"markdown":"These tests protect state normalization at the boundary between Hermes cron data and the desktop schedule model.","startLine":41,"endLine":